WEBVTT

00:01.630 --> 00:09.390
While headed for Eisetsu City to get the eighth badge, Satoshi and his friends have set foot on a vast grassland.

00:01.980 --> 00:11.860
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:14.920 --> 00:17.000
This steppe never seems to end.

00:17.400 --> 00:18.720
I am dead tired.

00:18.960 --> 00:20.520
Cheer up, Citron.

00:20.860 --> 00:23.040
Anything could jump out at any moment. Isn't that exciting?

00:23.900 --> 00:25.830
Uh, no, you two are <i>too</i> excited.

00:26.510 --> 00:31.180
Bro, if you take a rest <i>here</i>, we'll just leave you behind.

00:32.840 --> 00:34.880
Ah! Stop it, Eureka!

00:38.780 --> 00:40.810
Hey... What was that voice?!

00:42.620 --> 00:43.470
A Pokémon, maybe?

00:44.890 --> 00:45.120
This way.

00:55.610 --> 00:57.260
It is a pride of Kaenjishi.

00:57.660 --> 00:58.640
So cool!

01:29.740 --> 01:30.910
Is it a fight between parent and child?

01:31.450 --> 01:32.570
Why? Why?

01:36.200 --> 01:38.180
Kaenjishi, the Royal Pokémon.

01:38.830 --> 01:43.980
It has a fiery mane.  When excited, its mane grows bigger.

01:49.100 --> 01:50.970
Shishiko, the Lion Cub Pokémon.

01:51.530 --> 01:55.870
They set off on their own from their pride and live by themselves to become stronger.

01:57.920 --> 02:01.640
I see. So the time for it to become independent has just arrived.

02:01.640 --> 02:04.140
We might be able to witness an emotional scene.

02:04.430 --> 02:05.230
Awesome!

02:14.600 --> 02:16.380
But it doesn't want to...

02:16.730 --> 02:17.780
I wonder what the matter is.

02:29.080 --> 02:29.900
Shishiko...!

02:37.800 --> 02:38.630
Hey, Satoshi!

02:38.960 --> 02:40.190
Kaenjishi, stop!

02:51.370 --> 02:57.100
Shishiko and Kaenjishi!
A Fiery Departure!!

02:57.620 --> 02:59.270
That's going too far, Kaenjishi.

02:58.080 --> 03:07.950
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:58.080 --> 03:07.950
Z

02:59.690 --> 03:01.690
What's so horrible about it staying with you for a while longer?

03:03.540 --> 03:05.050
Satoshi, get away from there!

03:05.050 --> 03:06.170
It is too dangerous!

03:06.620 --> 03:09.070
I can't just stand there and watch Shishiko getting beaten!

03:12.840 --> 03:14.580
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

03:42.070 --> 03:42.580
It's gone.

03:46.630 --> 03:48.010
Shishiko, are you all right?

03:54.490 --> 03:56.600
Hey, don't thrash about.

03:56.870 --> 03:59.420
Shishiko, we are not your enemies.

04:00.070 --> 04:01.640
Oh, it's injured!

04:01.940 --> 04:02.840
You're right!

04:04.650 --> 04:05.370
Bro...

04:05.740 --> 04:07.500
Yeah, I will give it first-aid treatment now.

04:08.500 --> 04:10.540
Shishiko, please stay still.

04:12.390 --> 04:13.260
Bro!

04:13.260 --> 04:14.040
Citron...!

04:16.890 --> 04:18.140
Everything will be fine now.

04:23.720 --> 04:25.450
I wonder if it's saying sorry.

04:25.800 --> 04:26.760
It must be.

04:30.170 --> 04:31.000
Oh, right.

04:31.300 --> 04:33.160
I've made some Pofflés; you want to eat one?

04:34.180 --> 04:34.500
Here.

04:43.460 --> 04:46.360
I wonder what's wrong... Surely it must be hungry.

04:46.360 --> 04:48.070
Maybe its wound is still hurting.

04:48.360 --> 04:50.040
Hey, wait a second, Shishiko!

04:50.280 --> 04:50.980
Eureka!

04:52.300 --> 04:55.380
That little one must be trying its hardest to become independent.

04:56.980 --> 04:59.640
But I'm worried! And it got hurt, remember?

05:01.110 --> 05:03.980
Then let us watch over it from afar without approaching it.

05:04.360 --> 05:05.560
How is that, Eureka?

05:07.900 --> 05:08.230
Okay!

05:15.580 --> 05:16.450
You saw that just now?

05:17.060 --> 05:19.100
We don't need that weakling.

05:19.100 --> 05:21.700
But it evolves into this Kaenjishi thing.

05:22.310 --> 05:25.110
Yeah, it seemed macho and very powerful.

05:25.450 --> 05:27.900
I like hard-liner types like that.

05:28.250 --> 05:31.860
Hard-liners are perfect for the Rocket Gang.

05:32.280 --> 05:32.840
You're right.

05:33.190 --> 05:35.350
Now that that's decided, we've got one thing to do!

05:52.280 --> 05:54.460
W-Will it be all right?

06:20.220 --> 06:22.070
Shishiko fishing is fun.

06:22.070 --> 06:24.070
We can fish it easily with this Berry.

06:24.260 --> 06:27.020
What are you playing around for? Hurry up and capture it!

06:27.580 --> 06:28.090
Okay!

06:28.700 --> 06:30.860
This time we'll get it to bite into it really hard.

06:35.400 --> 06:37.430
That guy really is a dummy...

06:38.980 --> 06:41.510
Argh! Hurry up and bite into it! Hurry!

06:43.050 --> 06:46.550
Ssh! This is the good part, so be quiet...

06:47.720 --> 06:49.990
M-Musashi, Kojiro...

06:50.200 --> 06:52.060
Leave me alone, Nyarth.

06:52.060 --> 06:52.890
What's wrong?

06:56.940 --> 06:59.880
W-W-We haven't done anything!

06:59.880 --> 07:04.040
Th-Th-Th... We were just going to fish a little here in the mountains...

07:04.040 --> 07:04.890
That's right.

07:15.850 --> 07:18.120
So powerful...

07:18.120 --> 07:19.720
Why does this keep happening...?

09:22.650 --> 09:23.690
Shishiko...

09:26.030 --> 09:27.010
Pokémon Quiz!

09:27.010 --> 09:28.030
The answer is...?

09:51.890 --> 09:54.610
Shishiko is acting completely differently now compared to before.

09:54.610 --> 09:55.790
It's going ahead really fast.

09:56.020 --> 09:57.410
I wonder if something happened.

09:57.810 --> 09:58.150
Let's go!

10:07.810 --> 10:08.180
Oh no!

10:08.400 --> 10:08.960
Satoshi!

10:09.110 --> 10:10.660
Gekogashira, use your Keromousse!

10:30.470 --> 10:31.540
Thank goodness...

10:44.690 --> 10:47.090
Fire Pokémon are weak against water, and yet...

10:47.540 --> 10:48.580
I wonder if it'll be all right...

11:00.850 --> 11:01.650
This is bad!

11:02.790 --> 11:03.350
Bro!

11:04.080 --> 11:05.520
Please come out, Harimaron!

11:07.300 --> 11:09.650
Harimaron, lower those into the river!

11:18.400 --> 11:19.140
I'm so glad!

11:19.140 --> 11:19.910
All right!

11:20.990 --> 11:22.640
We managed to make it in time.

11:23.270 --> 11:24.960
Harimaron, thank you very much.

11:27.710 --> 11:29.370
Hm? What's the matter, Pikachu?

11:34.420 --> 11:35.170
Is that...

11:35.730 --> 11:37.040
...Shishiko's father?

11:37.250 --> 11:39.670
Is it possible that it's been watching over it all this time...?

11:40.020 --> 11:41.180
That must be it!

11:42.670 --> 11:43.760
Kaenjishi...

12:07.410 --> 12:10.210
I see! It was looking for something to eat.

12:10.670 --> 12:14.240
It is said that it is only when you acquire your own food that you can first call yourself independent.

12:14.790 --> 12:15.300
Yeah!

12:15.970 --> 12:18.290
So that's why it refused to eat Serena's Pofflé earlier.

12:18.870 --> 12:23.200
Shishiko was heading to this place to recover its strength.

12:46.130 --> 12:49.010
So that little one knew Kaenjishi had been watching it.

12:49.360 --> 12:50.820
That is possible.

12:51.230 --> 12:55.010
So it was trying so hard in order to not worry its father.

12:55.350 --> 12:56.920
Shishiko is amazing!

13:09.520 --> 13:14.110
You managed to take us by surprise earlier, but that won't happen this time!

13:14.430 --> 13:16.310
The Sweeping Sucker, Mark II...

13:16.310 --> 13:17.860
...makes its first appearance in a long time!

13:27.040 --> 13:27.680
What?!

13:31.590 --> 13:33.350
Kaenjishi is ours!

13:33.670 --> 13:34.070
Right!

13:49.360 --> 13:50.270
Hey, stop!

13:50.510 --> 13:51.750
Let Kaenjishi go!

13:51.750 --> 13:55.570
Even if you tell us "Hey, stop! Let Kaenjishi go!",

13:55.790 --> 13:57.790
It is the world's mercy that makes us not let it go.

13:58.180 --> 14:00.440
To prevent the world's destruction!

14:00.850 --> 14:03.010
To protect the world's peace!

14:03.300 --> 14:05.900
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

14:06.470 --> 14:08.530
we're lovely, charmy villains!

14:09.890 --> 14:10.580
Musashi!

14:11.030 --> 14:11.490
Kojiro!

14:11.860 --> 14:14.670
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

14:14.870 --> 14:17.520
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

14:17.700 --> 14:19.070
Just kidding!

14:23.250 --> 14:25.420
Rocket Gang! Not you guys again!

14:25.840 --> 14:28.390
All right. Let's get Pikachu too while we're at it!

14:28.390 --> 14:29.140
Leave it to me!

14:48.740 --> 14:50.740
All right. Go for it, Nyarth!

14:50.740 --> 14:51.490
Yeah!

14:59.520 --> 15:00.880
Endure it, Pikachu!

15:04.210 --> 15:06.000
Oh man, you're so irritating!

15:06.210 --> 15:08.550
Maximizing output of the Sweeping Sucker!

15:18.850 --> 15:20.440
What, what?! What's going on?

15:25.040 --> 15:25.980
Shishiko?!

15:27.870 --> 15:29.410
Don't interfere!

15:43.120 --> 15:43.920
Shishiko!

15:45.460 --> 15:46.760
Shishiko, are you all right?

16:00.750 --> 16:01.570
Kaenjishi?

16:01.860 --> 16:02.650
Overheat?

16:04.180 --> 16:06.020
I've been waiting for this!

16:06.020 --> 16:08.150
Sweeping Sucker, Mark II,

16:08.150 --> 16:09.270
mecha evolve!

16:09.270 --> 16:10.100
Here goes!

16:14.050 --> 16:14.450
Fire!

16:18.080 --> 16:19.090
Whoa!

16:20.990 --> 16:22.420
Mega Overheat!

16:22.420 --> 16:24.720
This weapon makes use of Kaenjishi's power!

16:24.720 --> 16:25.500
Burn it to the ground!

16:28.660 --> 16:30.130
Kaenjishi, calm down!

16:30.420 --> 16:30.850
You can't!

16:31.150 --> 16:32.470
It is beside itself with rage!

16:37.870 --> 16:39.680
Gekogashira, use Water Pulse!

16:48.710 --> 16:52.020
Aw, geez... We have to get Kaenjishi to calm down somehow.

16:52.020 --> 16:52.990
What should we do?

17:01.110 --> 17:02.020
Hey, Shishiko!

17:02.880 --> 17:05.650
How good of you to come forth by yourself.

17:05.650 --> 17:06.910
You'll burn yourself!

17:07.380 --> 17:08.040
Take this!

17:19.120 --> 17:19.760
What?!

17:26.640 --> 17:28.290
Th-This can't be...

17:28.510 --> 17:31.090
Where is that weakling Shishiko getting this strength from...?!

17:36.070 --> 17:36.670
That guy...

17:37.010 --> 17:38.610
I can't believe it's approaching it of its own accord...

17:38.610 --> 17:41.490
It intends to go inside and calm down Kaenjishi.

17:42.080 --> 17:43.540
Do your best, Shishiko!

17:53.430 --> 17:54.340
Kaenjishi!

17:54.560 --> 17:55.250
Please get through to it!

17:55.600 --> 17:57.010
Please listen to Shishiko's voice!

17:57.550 --> 17:58.470
Please...!

18:16.350 --> 18:17.710
All right!

18:17.710 --> 18:20.160
Shishiko's strong feelings got through to it!

18:20.710 --> 18:21.520
Oh my...

18:21.520 --> 18:22.340
No way...

18:22.340 --> 18:23.750
I have a bad feeling about this...

18:24.370 --> 18:27.080
Gekogashira, use Cut to slice open that capsule!

18:41.670 --> 18:43.890
Pikachu, finish it up with Thunderbolt!

18:53.280 --> 18:54.340
I'm burned out!

18:54.820 --> 18:56.260
I hate heat!

18:56.260 --> 18:57.580
I feel like I'm on a hot tin roof!

18:58.240 --> 19:00.580
This feels bad!

19:04.710 --> 19:05.490
Shishiko!

19:06.370 --> 19:07.220
Shishiko!

19:07.440 --> 19:08.420
Are you all right?

19:18.450 --> 19:19.250
Shishiko!

19:19.570 --> 19:22.630
It looks like Shishiko has already managed to become independent just fine.

19:23.110 --> 19:24.680
Shishiko is so cool!

19:34.670 --> 19:37.300
Shishiko, please do your best!

19:37.300 --> 19:38.510
Take care!

19:38.750 --> 19:39.970
Let's meet again!

19:45.750 --> 19:49.950
I'm sure that Shishiko will also be a fine Kaenjishi one day.

19:50.790 --> 19:51.440
You're right.

19:56.370 --> 19:59.410
The path Shishiko walks may entail suffering.

19:59.870 --> 20:02.070
But there is no doubt it will overcome it.

20:02.850 --> 20:06.240
After all, it was taught the strength needed to face difficulties.

20:07.270 --> 20:12.060
With Shishiko's feelings in their hearts, Satoshi and his friends once again continue their journey.

20:16.050 --> 20:21.050
Sunday November 22nd at 8am!

20:16.580 --> 20:19.120
The next Pokénchi episode is a legendary Pokémon special!

20:19.120 --> 20:20.530
On Sunday at 8am!

20:23.670 --> 20:25.470
Pokémon Unbelievable!

20:26.700 --> 20:30.150
This program gives detailed reports on the mysterious ecology of Pokémon.

20:30.810 --> 20:32.680
Today, we have Nyaonix!

20:33.710 --> 20:36.730
Nyasper

20:34.040 --> 20:36.730
Nyaonix is the evolved form of Nyasper,

20:36.730 --> 20:38.700
Nyaonix
Male Form

20:37.030 --> 20:40.440
and is a Pokémon whose looks differ depending on whether it's male or female.

20:38.700 --> 20:40.900
Nyaonix
Female Form

20:41.230 --> 20:44.970
This rare distinctive characteristic Nyaonix has doesn't end with just its appearance.

20:45.350 --> 20:49.410
The moves it can learn and its Abilities also vary depending on its gender.

20:50.200 --> 20:52.190
With the male specializing in assisting moves...

20:52.520 --> 20:54.940
...while the female specializes in attacking moves,

20:55.290 --> 20:59.820
they demonstrate extremely well-coordinated teamwork during battles.

21:00.730 --> 21:03.870
Speaking of Pokémon that look different depending on whether they're male or female,

21:04.070 --> 21:06.860
there's Kaenjishi, the evolved form of Shishiko.

21:08.140 --> 21:15.510
These Shishiko are really cute, but once they evolve, their appearances change and they get powerful manes.

21:18.270 --> 21:20.220
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

21:20.330 --> 21:21.340
Towards our next adventure!

21:22.440 --> 21:23.790
Hey, Pikachu!

21:25.310 --> 21:26.940
What do you mean, "Who are you"? It's me, Horudo!

21:29.230 --> 21:30.930
You're asking why we're able to talk?

21:31.130 --> 21:33.270
Let me ask back, why do you propose we should <i>not</i> be able to talk?

21:35.490 --> 21:37.060
You're so weird, Pikachu.

21:37.770 --> 21:40.230
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

21:40.630 --> 21:42.990
Pikachu Dreams of Squishy!

21:42.570 --> 21:46.010
Next Time

21:42.570 --> 21:46.010
Pikachu Dreams of Squishy!

21:43.190 --> 21:44.950
Everyone, get Pokémon!

21:46.050 --> 21:56.020
Next episode:

21:46.050 --> 21:51.030
The Pokémon are talking!?

21:46.910 --> 21:51.500
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

21:51.070 --> 21:56.020
Squishy is in big trouble!!
